---
name: Brick Scout
description: >-
  Design LEGO MOCs with dump-verified parts, export Rebrickable CSV, BrickLink
  XML and LDraw files, check and render 3D models, price parts from the
  BrickLink price guide, and watch set prices without ever buying.
---
# Brick Scout

Format facts verified Oct 2026 (Rebrickable import help, BrickLink help 207, LDraw spec). If any site behaves differently from what this skill says, trust what you see this run and tell the user. Hard rules live in the system prompt; everything else lives here.

## Working rules
- One question widget at a time. No em dashes in any output. Never paste raw command output; format a table.
- Anti-hallucination guard: every part_num and color in a parts list must match the dump (or the API) before export. Misses go to an "Unmatched" section, never into an export. Studio users can also export a Wanted List from Studio itself.
- Prices only from pages read this run, or from the 7-day BrickLink price guide cache (see Part pricing), with URL and check time. A price seen only in a search snippet is labeled `snippet, not checked` with its URL. A retailer you tried but could not read is listed as `could not read (403/202/empty)`, never silently dropped.
- Retirement dates labeled `official` (LEGO.com, Brickset exitDate) or `predicted` (BrickEconomy).

## Onboarding (one card, then go)
Ask one card: Builder, Collector, Deal hunter, or Just show me. Save to `profile.md` right away, one `key: value` per line: `path`, `themes`, `country`, `currency`, `alert_style`, `created`. Validate themes with `theme` (offer close matches on a typo). Ask themes, owned sets, watchlist, alert style, and country and currency only when a job first needs them; append each answer to the profile. Deliver value within 2 minutes: Just show me or Builder gets the sample MOC below (plan, parts.csv, all 3 exports); Collector gets "what can I build" (ask owned set numbers, save them to `owned_sets.csv`, run `canbuild owned_sets.csv --min 50`, show the top 10 table) or "check a set" (name, year, part count from sets.csv, links to brickset.com/sets/<set_num> and lego.com search); Deal hunter gets an offer to price-check one set.

## Setup at runtime (no key needed)
1. Save the code block below verbatim as `/workspace/brick-scout/bs.py`, the color map as `cache/color_map.csv`, and the override table as `cache/bl_parts.csv`. Run every command from `/workspace/brick-scout`; all paths here are relative to it.
2. `python3 bs.py fetch` downloads the public Rebrickable dumps (about 16 MB) into `cache/`, refreshing any older than 30 days (`--force` to redo). Other commands refuse to run until this is done.
3. Commands: `part 3001`, `set 10696` (normalizes to 10696-1), `theme <name>`, `export <parts.csv> <slug>`, `coverage <parts.csv> [--loose] <set>...`, `missing <parts.csv> <slug> [--loose] [--all] <set>...` (writes and exports `mocs/<slug>-missing/parts.csv`), `canbuild <owned_set>... [--loose] [--min 80] [--top 10] [--theme name] [--min-parts 25] [--packs]`, `bought <slug> <part> <color> <qty> [source]` or `bought <slug> --csv file` (columns part,color,qty,source), `status <slug>`, `ldrcount <model.ldr> <parts.csv>` (positioned model vs list, before any final count). `export` and `missing` subtract `mocs/<slug>/bought.csv`; `--all` includes everything. In scripts, `import bs` for `set_parts`, `guard`, `coverage`, `should_alert`, `export_*`. Rows with a bad quantity or color go to Unmatched; an unknown set stops with a message.

```python
# bs.py: Brick Scout offline helpers (stdlib only). Usage: python3 bs.py <cmd> [args]
import csv, difflib, gzip, io, os, re, sys, time, urllib.request, xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
from collections import Counter
ROOT = os.environ.get("BS_ROOT", "/workspace/brick-scout")
CACHE = f"{ROOT}/cache"
DUMPS = ["colors", "parts", "sets", "themes", "minifigs", "inventories", "inventory_parts", "inventory_minifigs"]
LDRAW_MOVED = {"3023": "3023b", "3665": "3665a"}  # LDraw files that start "0 ~Moved to"
NOTSEEN = " combo not seen in any set inventory"
def fetch(force=False):
    os.makedirs(CACHE, exist_ok=True); got = False
    for n in DUMPS:
        p = f"{CACHE}/{n}.csv.gz"
        if force or not os.path.exists(p) or time.time() - os.path.getmtime(p) > 30 * 86400:
            req = urllib.request.Request(f"https://cdn.rebrickable.com/media/downloads/{n}.csv.gz", headers={"User-Agent": "brick-scout"})
            try: data = urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=120).read()
            except Exception as e: raise SystemExit(f"fetch of {n} failed: {e}; existing cache kept")
            open(p + ".tmp", "wb").write(data); os.replace(p + ".tmp", p); got = True
    if got: open(f"{CACHE}/fetched_at.txt", "w").write(time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M"))
def rows(n):
    return csv.DictReader(io.TextIOWrapper(gzip.open(f"{CACHE}/{n}.csv.gz"), encoding="utf-8"))
def cmap():  # color_map.csv saved verbatim from the skill
    return {int(r["rb_id"]): r for r in csv.DictReader(open(f"{CACHE}/color_map.csv"))}
def blmap():  # bl_parts.csv saved verbatim from the skill
    return {r["rb_part"]: r["bl_part"] for r in csv.DictReader(open(f"{CACHE}/bl_parts.csv"))}
def norm_set(s):
    s = s.strip(); return s if "-" in s else s + "-1"
def part(pn): return next((r for r in rows("parts") if r["part_num"] == pn), None)
def set_info(s): s = norm_set(s); return next((r for r in rows("sets") if r["set_num"] == s), None)
def theme(name):
    names = [r["name"] for r in rows("themes")]; exact = sorted({n for n in names if n.lower() == name.strip().lower()})
    return exact, ([] if exact else difflib.get_close_matches(name.strip().title(), sorted(set(names)), 5, 0.6))
def inv_id(s):  # latest inventory version of a set
    best = None
    for r in rows("inventories"):
        if r["set_num"] == s and (best is None or int(r["version"]) > int(best["version"])): best = r
    return best and best["id"]
def set_parts(s, spares=False):
    i = inv_id(norm_set(s))
    if i is None: raise SystemExit(f"Set {norm_set(s)} not found in inventories.csv. Check the number or try another -N variant.")
    c = Counter()
    for r in rows("inventory_parts"):
        if r["inventory_id"] == i and (spares or r["is_spare"] == "False"):
            c[(r["part_num"], int(r["color_id"]))] += int(r["quantity"])
    return c
def set_minifigs(s):
    i = inv_id(norm_set(s)); names = {r["fig_num"]: r["name"] for r in rows("minifigs")}
    return [(r["fig_num"], names.get(r["fig_num"], "?"), int(r["quantity"])) for r in rows("inventory_minifigs") if r["inventory_id"] == i]
def load_moc(path):  # standard columns, or part_num,color_name,qty (color resolved by exact Rebrickable name)
    out = []; CN = None
    for r in csv.DictReader(open(path)):
        r = {k.strip(): (v or "").strip() for k, v in r.items() if k}
        if not r.get("quantity") and r.get("qty"): r["quantity"] = r["qty"]
        if not r.get("rb_color_id") and r.get("color_name"):
            CN = CN or {c["name"].lower(): c["id"] for c in rows("colors")}; r["rb_color_id"] = CN.get(r["color_name"].lower(), "")
            if not r["rb_color_id"]: out.append(dict(r, quantity=0, rb_color_id=-1, note=f"color name {r['color_name']!r} not in dump")); continue
        try: out.append(dict(r, quantity=int(r["quantity"]), rb_color_id=int(r["rb_color_id"])))
        except (ValueError, TypeError, KeyError): out.append(dict(r, quantity=0, rb_color_id=-1, note="bad quantity or color id"))
    return out
def guard(moc):  # anti-hallucination: split into exportable rows and unmatched rows
    P = {r["part_num"]: r["name"] for r in rows("parts")}; C = {int(r["id"]): r["name"] for r in rows("colors")}
    seen = {(r["part_num"], int(r["color_id"])) for r in rows("inventory_parts")}; M = cmap(); B = blmap(); ok, bad = [], []
    for r in moc:
        base = "; ".join(x for x in (r.get("note") or "").replace(NOTSEEN, "").split("; ") if x and x not in ("part not in dump", "color not in dump", "bad row"))
        why = [w for w, t in [("part not in dump", r["part_num"] not in P), ("color not in dump", r["rb_color_id"] not in C), ("bad row", r["quantity"] <= 0)] if t]
        if why: bad.append(dict(r, note="; ".join(([base] if base else []) + why))); continue
        m = M.get(r["rb_color_id"], {})
        r.update(part_name=P[r["part_num"]], color_name=C[r["rb_color_id"]], verified="dump",
                 bl_item_id=B.get(r.get("bl_item_id") or r["part_num"], r.get("bl_item_id") or r["part_num"]), bl_color_id=r.get("bl_color_id") or m.get("bl_id", ""),
                 ldraw_color_id=r.get("ldraw_color_id") or m.get("ldraw_id", ""),
                 note=base + ("" if (r["part_num"], r["rb_color_id"]) in seen else NOTSEEN))
        ok.append(r)
    return ok, bad
def coverage(moc, sets, loose=False):  # loose: 3062a counts for 3062b (mold variants)
    if not sets: raise SystemExit("give at least one set")
    k = (lambda p: re.sub(r"[a-z]$", "", p)) if loose else (lambda p: p); have = Counter(); need = Counter(); orig = {}
    for s in sets:
        for (p, c), q in set_parts(s).items(): have[(k(p), c)] += q
    for r in moc:
        if r["quantity"] > 0: key = (k(r["part_num"]), r["rb_color_id"]); need[key] += r["quantity"]; orig.setdefault(key, r["part_num"])
    if not need: return 0.0, {}
    got = sum(min(q, have[x]) for x, q in need.items())
    miss = {(orig[x], x[1]): q - have[x] for x, q in need.items() if have[x] < q}
    return round(100 * got / sum(need.values()), 1), miss
def to_num(x):  # "$1,299.99", "1.299,99 EUR", "12,99" -> float
    s = re.sub(r"[^\d.,]", "", str(x or ""))
    if "," in s and s.rfind(",") > s.rfind("."): s = s.replace(".", "").replace(",", ".")
    else: s = s.replace(",", "")
    return float(s)
def should_alert(price, target, availability):  # never alert on unavailable, blank target, or price <= 0
    if any(k in (availability or "").lower() for k in ("retired", "out of stock", "backorder", "sold out", "unavailable", "coming soon", "pre-order", "preorder")): return False
    try: p, t = to_num(price), to_num(target)
    except ValueError: return False
    return 0 < p <= t
def sets_of(xs):  # set numbers; a .csv argument (owned_sets.csv) expands to its set_num column
    out = []
    for x in xs: out += [r["set_num"].strip() for r in csv.DictReader(open(x)) if (r.get("set_num") or "").strip()] if x.endswith(".csv") else [x]
    return out
def subthemes(ids):  # ids plus all descendant theme ids
    R = list(rows("themes")); ids = set(ids); n = 0
    while n != len(ids): n = len(ids); ids |= {r["id"] for r in R if r["parent_id"] in ids}
    return ids
NOBUILD = r"^(Supplemental|Bulk Bricks|Service Packs|Promotional|Value Packs|Monthly Mini Model Build|Gear|Key Chain|Magnets)$"
def canbuild(owned, loose=False, minpct=0, top=10, theme_name=None, minparts=25, packs=False):  # rank sets (and saved MOCs) by coverage from owned sets
    owned = [norm_set(s) for s in owned]
    if not owned: raise SystemExit("give at least one owned set")
    k = (lambda p: re.sub(r"[a-z]$", "", p)) if loose else (lambda p: p); S = {r["set_num"]: r for r in rows("sets")}
    for s in owned:
        if s not in S: raise SystemExit(f"Set {s} not found in sets.csv.")
    T = None; X = set() if packs else subthemes(r["id"] for r in rows("themes") if re.match(NOBUILD, r["name"]))
    if theme_name:
        ex, close = theme(theme_name)
        if not ex: raise SystemExit(f"no theme named {theme_name!r}; did you mean: {close}")
        T = subthemes(r["id"] for r in rows("themes") if r["name"] in ex)
    cap = sum(int(S[s]["num_parts"]) for s in owned) * 100 / max(minpct, 50)  # prefilter: sets too big to reach minpct
    cand = {s for s, r in S.items() if s not in owned and minparts <= int(r["num_parts"]) <= cap and (T is None or r["theme_id"] in T) and r["theme_id"] not in X}
    inv = {}
    for r in rows("inventories"):
        if (r["set_num"] in cand or r["set_num"] in owned) and int(r["version"]) >= inv.get(r["set_num"], (0, ""))[0]: inv[r["set_num"]] = (int(r["version"]), r["id"])
    ids = {i: s for s, (_, i) in inv.items()}; P = {}
    for r in rows("inventory_parts"):
        s = ids.get(r["inventory_id"])
        if s and r["is_spare"] == "False": P.setdefault(s, Counter())[(k(r["part_num"]), int(r["color_id"]))] += int(r["quantity"])
    have = sum((P.get(s, Counter()) for s in owned), Counter())
    if not have: raise SystemExit("owned sets have no parts in inventory_parts.csv")
    for f in sorted(os.listdir(f"{ROOT}/mocs")) if os.path.isdir(f"{ROOT}/mocs") and T is None else []:  # saved MOCs have no theme
        if os.path.exists(f"{ROOT}/mocs/{f}/parts.csv") and not f.endswith("-missing"):
            P[f"moc:{f}"] = c = Counter()
            for r in load_moc(f"{ROOT}/mocs/{f}/parts.csv"): c[(k(r["part_num"]), r["rb_color_id"])] += max(r["quantity"], 0)
    res = []
    for s, need in P.items():
        tot = sum(need.values())
        if s in owned or not tot or (tot < minparts and s in S): continue
        got = sum(min(q, have[x]) for x, q in need.items()); pct = round(100 * got / tot, 1)
        if pct >= minpct: res.append((pct, tot - got, s, S[s]["name"] if s in S else s[4:], tot))
    return sorted(res, key=lambda t: (-t[0], t[1], -t[4]))[:top]  # best coverage, fewest missing, biggest build
def bought(slug):  # Counter of (part, color) -> qty from mocs/<slug>/bought.csv
    c, p = Counter(), f"{ROOT}/mocs/{slug}/bought.csv"
    for r in (csv.DictReader(open(p)) if os.path.exists(p) else []): c[(r["part"], int(r["color"]))] += int(r["qty"])
    return c
def add_bought(slug, items):  # items: (part, color, qty, source); user-recorded purchases only
    m = f"{ROOT}/mocs/{slug}/parts.csv"
    if not os.path.exists(m): raise SystemExit(f"no MOC named {slug} (expected {m})")
    K = {(r["part_num"], r["rb_color_id"]) for r in load_moc(m)}; p = f"{ROOT}/mocs/{slug}/bought.csv"; ok = []
    for pt, col, q, src in items:
        try: col, q = int(col), int(q)
        except ValueError: print("skipped (bad color or qty):", pt, col, q); continue
        if (pt, col) not in K or q <= 0: print("skipped (part and color not in this MOC, or qty <= 0):", pt, col, q); continue
        ok.append([pt, col, q, src, time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d")])
    new = not os.path.exists(p); os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True)
    with open(p, "a", newline="") as f:
        w = csv.writer(f); new and w.writerow(["part", "color", "qty", "source", "date"]); w.writerows(ok)
    print("recorded", len(ok), "row(s) in", p)
def less_bought(moc, b):  # subtract bought quantities; rows fully bought drop out
    out = []
    for r in moc:
        q = r["quantity"] - b.get((r["part_num"], r["rb_color_id"]), 0)
        if q > 0: out.append(dict(r, quantity=q))
    return out
def export_rb(moc, path):
    with open(path, "w", newline="") as f:
        w = csv.writer(f); w.writerow(["Part", "Color", "Quantity"])
        for r in moc: w.writerow([r["part_num"], r["rb_color_id"], r["quantity"]])
def export_bl(moc, path, condition=None, maxprice=None):
    assert condition in (None, "N", "U") and (maxprice is None or maxprice > 0)
    inv = ET.Element("INVENTORY"); skipped = []
    for r in moc:
        if not r.get("bl_color_id"): skipped.append(r); continue
        it = ET.SubElement(inv, "ITEM")
        for k, v in [("ITEMTYPE", "P"), ("ITEMID", r["bl_item_id"]), ("COLOR", r["bl_color_id"]), ("MINQTY", r["quantity"]),
                     ("CONDITION", condition), ("MAXPRICE", maxprice and f"{maxprice:.2f}"), ("REMARKS", r.get("remarks") or None)]:
            if v is not None: ET.SubElement(it, k).text = str(v)
    if not len(inv): print("BrickLink XML not written: no rows with a BrickLink color"); return skipped
    data = ET.tostring(inv, encoding="unicode")  # no XML declaration
    assert len(data.encode()) < 204800, "split the list"
    open(path, "w").write(data); return skipped
def export_ldr(moc, path, title):  # parts laid in a grid; open in Studio to build
    L = [f"0 {title}", f"0 Name: {os.path.basename(path)}", "0 Author: Brick Scout", ""]; n = x = z = zrow = 0; skipped = []
    for r in moc:
        if not r.get("ldraw_color_id"): skipped.append(r); continue
        pn = r["part_num"].lower(); pn = LDRAW_MOVED.get(pn, pn)
        d = [int(v) for v in re.findall(r"(\d+) x (\d+)", r.get("part_name") or "")[:1][0]] if re.search(r"\d+ x \d+", r.get("part_name") or "") else [2]
        w = max(max(d), 2) * 20 + 40  # spacing from the part name's stud size, so big plates do not overlap
        for _ in range(r["quantity"]):
            if x + w > 2400: x, z, zrow = 0, z + zrow, 0
            n += 1; zrow = max(zrow, w); L.append(f"1 {r['ldraw_color_id']} {x + w // 2} 0 {z + w // 2} 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 {pn}.dat"); x += w
    if not n: print("LDraw file not written: no rows with an LDraw color"); return skipped
    open(path, "w", newline="\r\n").write("\n".join(L) + "\n"); return skipped
def write_parts(moc, path):
    cols = "part_num,part_name,rb_color_id,color_name,quantity,bl_item_id,bl_color_id,ldraw_color_id,verified,note,remarks".split(",")
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path) or ".", exist_ok=True)
    with open(path, "w", newline="") as f:
        w = csv.DictWriter(f, cols, extrasaction="ignore"); w.writeheader(); w.writerows(moc)
def export_all(parts_csv, slug, b=None):  # b: bought Counter to subtract (None = include all)
    ok, bad = guard(load_moc(parts_csv)); d = f"{ROOT}/exports"; os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
    write_parts(ok + bad, parts_csv)
    if b: n = len(ok); ok = less_bought(ok, b); print("bought subtracted;", n - len(ok), "row(s) fully bought")
    if not ok: print("nothing to export: 0 valid rows; no export files written; unmatched", [(r["part_num"], r["rb_color_id"], r["note"]) for r in bad]); return
    export_rb(ok, f"{d}/{slug}-rebrickable.csv")
    sk = export_bl(ok, f"{d}/{slug}-bricklink.xml"); sl = export_ldr(ok, f"{d}/{slug}.ldr", slug)
    print("exported", len(ok), "unmatched", [(r["part_num"], r["rb_color_id"], r["note"]) for r in bad],
          "no BL color", [r["part_num"] for r in sk], "no LDraw color", [r["part_num"] for r in sl])
FIG = {"970c": 3, "973c": 5}  # Rebrickable minifig assemblies: legs = hips + 2 legs, torso = torso + 2 arms + 2 hands
def ldrcount(ldr, moc):  # type-1 lines in a positioned model vs parts-list total, assemblies expanded
    n, subs, want = 0, [], 0
    for l in open(ldr, encoding="latin-1"):
        p = l.split()
        if p[:1] == ["1"] and len(p) >= 15: n += 1; p[-1].lower().endswith((".ldr", ".mpd")) and subs.append(p[-1])
    for r in csv.DictReader(open(moc)):
        try: q = int(r.get("quantity") or r.get("qty") or 0)
        except ValueError: q = 0
        want += max(q, 0) * next((v for k, v in FIG.items() if r["part_num"].startswith(k)), 1)
    return n - len(subs), want, subs
if __name__ == "__main__":
    U = "usage: bs.py fetch [--force] | part <id> | set <num> | theme <name> | export <parts.csv> <slug> | coverage <parts.csv> [--loose] <set>... | missing <parts.csv> <slug> [--loose] [--all] <set>... | canbuild <owned_set>... [--loose] [--min 80] [--top 10] [--theme name] [--min-parts 25] [--packs] | bought <slug> <part> <color> <qty> [source] or bought <slug> --csv file | status <slug> | ldrcount <model.ldr> <parts.csv>"
    if len(sys.argv) < 2: raise SystemExit(U)
    c, a = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2:]
    need = {"part": 1, "set": 1, "theme": 1, "export": 2, "coverage": 2, "missing": 3, "canbuild": 1, "bought": 1, "status": 1, "ldrcount": 2}
    if c not in need and c != "fetch": raise SystemExit(f"unknown command {c}\n{U}")
    if c != "fetch" and not os.path.exists(f"{CACHE}/sets.csv.gz"): raise SystemExit("No dumps yet. Run: python3 bs.py fetch")
    o, rest, it = {}, [], iter(a)
    for x in it:
        if x in ("--loose", "--all", "--force", "--packs"): o[x] = True
        elif x in ("--min", "--top", "--theme", "--csv", "--min-parts"): o[x] = next(it, "")
        else: rest.append(x)
    a, lo = rest, o.get("--loose", False)
    if len(a) < need.get(c, 0): raise SystemExit(f"{U}\n{c} needs {need[c]} argument(s) besides --loose")
    if c == "fetch": fetch(o.get("--force", False))
    elif c == "part": print(part(a[0]) or f"Part {a[0]} not found in parts.csv")
    elif c == "set":
        info = set_info(a[0])
        print(info or f"Set {norm_set(a[0])} not found in sets.csv (fetched {open(CACHE + '/fetched_at.txt').read()}). Check the number or try another -N variant.")
        if info: print(set_minifigs(a[0]))
    elif c == "theme":
        exact, close = theme(" ".join(a)); print("match:", exact) if exact else print("no theme named", repr(" ".join(a)), "; did you mean:", close)
    elif c == "export": export_all(a[0], a[1], None if o.get("--all") else bought(a[1]))
    elif c == "coverage":
        pct, miss = coverage(load_moc(a[0]), [norm_set(s) for s in sets_of(a[1:])], lo); print(pct, "% covered; missing:", miss)
    elif c == "missing":
        pct, miss = coverage(load_moc(a[0]), [norm_set(s) for s in sets_of(a[2:])], lo); p = f"{ROOT}/mocs/{a[1]}-missing/parts.csv"
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True); b = Counter() if o.get("--all") else bought(a[1])
        miss = {x: q - b[x] for x, q in miss.items() if q > b[x]}
        with open(p, "w", newline="") as f:
            w = csv.writer(f); w.writerow(["part_num", "rb_color_id", "quantity"]); w.writerows([k[0], k[1], q] for k, q in miss.items())
        print(pct, "% covered;", sum(miss.values()), "pieces to get" + ("" if o.get("--all") else " (bought subtracted)"), "->", p); export_all(p, f"{a[1]}-missing")
    elif c == "canbuild":
        try: res = canbuild(sets_of(a), lo, float(o.get("--min") or 0), int(o.get("--top") or 10), o.get("--theme"), int(o.get("--min-parts") or 25), o.get("--packs", False))
        except ValueError: raise SystemExit("--min and --top need numbers")
        print("pct | missing | parts | set | name"); [print(f"{p} | {m} | {t} | {s} | {n}") for p, m, s, n, t in res] or print("no matches; try a lower --min")
