## Core jobs
1. **MOC design**: input theme, photo, or size. Write `mocs/<slug>/plan.md` (concept, studs, palette, submodels, stages with goal, parts, tips) and `mocs/<slug>/parts.csv`:
`part_num,part_name,rb_color_id,color_name,quantity,bl_item_id,bl_color_id,ldraw_color_id,verified,note,remarks` (verified = dump, api, or no; remarks optional, goes to BrickLink REMARKS). Run the guard before showing a final list.
2. **Set lookup and minifigs**: normalize "10236" to "10236-1", read sets.csv (name, year, num_parts), list minifigs via inventory_minifigs.csv plus minifigs.csv. Never link brickset.com for a set that is not in sets.csv; Brickset shows an empty page instead of a 404.
3. **Exports** (`exports/`):
   - Rebrickable CSV `<slug>-rebrickable.csv`, header exactly `Part,Color,Quantity`, Rebrickable ids. External Source stays Rebrickable on import.
   - BrickLink Wanted List XML `<slug>-bricklink.xml`: no XML declaration, root INVENTORY, ITEM with ITEMTYPE P, ITEMID, COLOR (BrickLink id), MINQTY; optional CONDITION only N or U, MAXPRICE only if greater than 0, REMARKS from a `remarks` column (auto-escaped). Under 204800 bytes, split if larger. ITEMID comes from the BrickLink override table (above), else the Rebrickable part_num. Rebrickable numbers ending in a letter often differ on BrickLink. Without a key, check unknown ids keylessly: fetch https://www.bricklink.com/v2/catalog/catalogitem.page?P=<id>; a title of 'BrickLink Page Not Found' means the id is wrong, and the correct item lists the old number under 'Alternate Item No'. Mark unchecked ids in the note. With a key, use the API `external_ids.BrickLink`. BrickLink's file-upload tab rejects .xml files (verified 2026-10-13), so tell the user to open https://www.bricklink.com/v2/wanted/upload.page, choose the 'Upload BrickLink XML format' tab, and paste the file's contents. Paste into a new, empty wanted list; uploading into a list that already has an item adds the quantities. Rows without a BrickLink color are listed, not exported.
   - LDraw `<slug>.ldr`: type-1 lines `1 <ldraw_color> x y z 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 <part>.dat`, parts laid in a grid. BrickLink Wanted List upload, Rebrickable import and BrickLink Studio all accept .ldr; Rebrickable CSV import (My LEGO, My Part Lists, Import Parts, From Disk) was verified 2026-10-13 and may swap retired molds for current ones (for example 4589 to 59900), which is fine; Studio renders 3D and can generate instructions.
   The user uploads files themselves.
4. **Build from your sets** (keyless): Save owned sets to `owned_sets.csv` (`set_num,qty,note`); any set argument may be that file. `canbuild` ranks official sets of at least 25 parts, skipping parts packs and promos (Supplemental, Bulk Bricks, Service Packs, Promotional, Value Packs, Monthly Mini Model Build, Gear; `--packs` includes them; `--min-parts` changes the size floor), and no bigger than the owned total scaled by --min (fast, about 5 s) and your saved MOCs (skipped when `--theme` is set) by coverage; Rebrickable dumps have no MOC inventories, so community MOCs need the API. Each MOC can have `bought.csv` (part,color,qty,source,date); only the user records purchases, never auto-buy; `status <slug>` shows needed, bought, remaining. `coverage` sums owned set inventories from inventory_parts.csv (spares excluded) and reports coverage % and missing parts; `missing` exports just the missing parts. Matching is exact-mold; use `--loose` (3062a counts for 3062b) or say an older mold may already be owned.
5. **Deal watchlist**: `watchlist.csv` `set_num,name,target_price,currency,retailers,last_price,last_source_url,last_checked,status_notes`; `prices.csv` `checked_at,set_num,retailer,price,currency,in_stock,url,source_type` (page or snippet).

## Part pricing (BrickLink price guide, checked 2026-10-14)
The price guide page `catalogPG.asp?P=<bl_id>&ColorID=<bl_color>` gives curl a 202 with an empty body and gives WebFetch a "verify you're not a robot" page, but it is readable in headless Chrome. On first use save the block below as `blpg.js`, run `npm init -y && npm i playwright-core` in `/workspace/brick-scout`, then `node blpg.js mocs/<slug>/parts.csv [--max N] [--refresh]` (run `bs.py export` first so BrickLink ids are filled). It waits 3 s between pages, retries a failed page once, caches each page in `cache/bl_pg/` for 7 days, stops the run on a robot check, tries the BrickLink id, the Rebrickable id, then the id without a trailing a or b, and writes `<parts>-prices.csv` (6-month sold and current stock Qty Avg Price, new and used, USD, with URL and check time) plus a "Not priced" list. About 6 s per uncached part. Show every Not priced row; never fill a gap with an estimate. Without Node, playwright-core or Chrome it exits saying so: report the parts as `could not read` and offer the BrickLink Wanted List upload, whose page shows prices.

```js
// blpg.js: BrickLink price guide reader (6-month sold and current stock, USD). Usage: node blpg.js <parts.csv> [--max N] [--refresh]
// Needs Node, playwright-core (npm i playwright-core) and Chrome or Chromium (CHROME=/path). Reads pages only; never buys or logs in.
const fs = require('fs'), path = require('path');
const A = process.argv.slice(2), file = A.find(a => !a.startsWith('--') && !/^\d+$/.test(a)), max = +(A[A.indexOf('--max') + 1] || 0) || 1e9;
if (!file || !fs.existsSync(file)) { console.log('usage: node blpg.js <parts.csv> [--max N] [--refresh]'); process.exit(1); }
const ROOT = process.env.BS_ROOT || '/workspace/brick-scout', CACHE = path.join(ROOT, 'cache/bl_pg'), DAY = 864e5, WAIT = 3000;
fs.mkdirSync(CACHE, { recursive: true });
function parseCSV(t) { const R = []; let row = [], f = '', q = false;
  for (let i = 0; i < t.length; i++) { const c = t[i];
    if (q) { if (c == '"' && t[i + 1] == '"') { f += '"'; i++; } else if (c == '"') q = false; else f += c; }
    else if (c == '"') q = true; else if (c == ',') { row.push(f); f = ''; } else if (c == '\n' || c == '\r') { if (c == '\r' && t[i + 1] == '\n') i++; row.push(f); R.push(row); row = []; f = ''; } else f += c; }
  if (f || row.length) { row.push(f); R.push(row); } const h = R.shift(); return R.filter(r => r.join('')).map(r => Object.fromEntries(h.map((k, i) => [k.trim(), (r[i] || '').trim()]))); }
const rows = parseCSV(fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8')).slice(0, max);
const COLS = ['sold_new', 'sold_used', 'stock_new', 'stock_used'], cell = s => /Unavailable/.test(s) ? null : { lots: +((s.match(/(?:Times Sold|Total Lots): (\d+)/) || [])[1] || 0), qty: +((s.match(/Total Qty: (\d+)/) || [])[1] || 0), qty_avg_usd: +((s.match(/Qty Avg Price: US \$([\d.,]+)/) || [])[1] || '0').replace(/,/g, '') };
(async () => {
  let chromium; try { ({ chromium } = require('playwright-core')); } catch { console.log('playwright-core not installed: run `npm i playwright-core` in this folder. Price guide: could not read.'); process.exit(2); }
  const exe = process.env.CHROME || ['/usr/bin/google-chrome', '/usr/bin/chromium', '/usr/bin/chromium-browser', '/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome'].find(fs.existsSync);
  if (!exe) { console.log('Chrome or Chromium not found (set CHROME=/path). Price guide: could not read.'); process.exit(2); }
  let b, ctx, last = 0, blocked = false; const out = [];
  async function page(url) {
    if (!b) { b = await chromium.launch({ executablePath: exe, args: ['--no-sandbox'] }); ctx = await b.newContext({ userAgent: 'Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0 Safari/537.36' }); }
    for (let t = 0; t < 2; t++) {
      const w = last + WAIT - Date.now(); if (w > 0) await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, w)); last = Date.now();
      const p = await ctx.newPage();
      try { await p.goto(url, { waitUntil: 'domcontentloaded', timeout: 30000 }); await p.waitForTimeout(4000);
        const r = await p.evaluate(() => { const tr = [...document.querySelectorAll('tr')].find(t => { const c = [...t.children].filter(x => x.tagName == 'TD'); return c.length == 4 && c.every(x => /Times Sold:|Total Lots:|Unavailable/.test(x.innerText)); });
          return { robot: /not a robot/i.test(document.body.innerText), title: document.title, cells: tr ? [...tr.children].map(x => x.innerText.replace(/\s+/g, ' ')) : null }; });
        await p.close(); return r;
      } catch (e) { await p.close().catch(() => {}); if (t) return { error: e.message }; }
    }
  }
  for (const r of rows) {
    const part = r.part_num, color = r.bl_color_id, ids = [...new Set([r.bl_item_id || part, part, part.replace(/[ab]$/, '')].filter(Boolean))];
    const rec = { part_num: part, color_name: r.color_name || '', bl_color_id: color, quantity: +(r.quantity || r.qty || 0), status: 'not_found', tried: [] };
    if (!color) { rec.status = 'no BrickLink color id'; out.push(rec); continue; }
    if (blocked) { rec.status = 'blocked'; out.push(rec); continue; }
    for (const id of ids) {
      const url = `https://www.bricklink.com/catalogPG.asp?P=${encodeURIComponent(id)}&ColorID=${color}`, cf = path.join(CACHE, `${id}_${color}.json`.replace(/[^\w.-]/g, '_'));
