## Optional keys and connectors
- REBRICKABLE_API_KEY (secret): `https://rebrickable.com/api/v3/`, header `Authorization: key $KEY`, at most 1 request/sec, on 429 wait. Use for BrickLink part ids, part-color confirmation, and alternate builds (`/lego/sets/<set>/alternates/`). Without it, the dumps cover everything else.
- BRICKSET_API_KEY (secret, free): official exitDate and price.
- Google Sheets (live watchlist), Gmail or Slack (alerts to self, set up on yes), Google Drive (save exports on yes). Otherwise files stay in /workspace.
- BrickLink API not used by default (needs the user's consumer key and token, IP allowlisted). BrickEconomy API is paid. Rebrickable has no prices.

## Routines (offer when relevant; create after a yes; notify only)
- **Daily price watch**: at most 3 watchlist sets per run (rotate the rest). Find the LEGO.com URL in the user's locale with WebSearch (`/en-us/`, `/en-gb/`, `/de-de/`... `product/<slug>-<setnum>`) and read it. Record the availability text. If the page says 'Retired Product', the shown price is not purchasable: set in_stock=no, status_notes=retired, and never alert. If 'Temporarily out of stock' or 'Backorder', record it and do not alert on the LEGO.com price. Use web search snippets for other retailers, labeled `snippet`. BrickEconomy set pages are readable with WebFetch (use for value and predicted retirement, labeled `page`). Rebrickable blocks curl (403) but WebFetch works. BrickLink price guide: see Part pricing. Walmart and Target block direct reads: use snippets. Alert only when `bs.should_alert(price, target, availability_text)` is true. If a price cannot be parsed, record `unparsed: <text>` in status_notes and say so in the report. Never compare a price to a target in another currency.
- **Weekly retiring soon**: LEGO.com retiring soon page: parse the embedded JSON (`productCode`, `name`, `formattedAmount`, `availabilityText`). Only the first 20 of N products are in the HTML and `?page=` does not help; report '20 of N read' and fill the rest from BrickEconomy's retiring-soon page (predicted). Brickset exitDate with a key; without a key, read 'Launch/exit' from brickset.com/sets/<set_num> per set (official; 't.b.a' means none announced). BrickEconomy retiring-soon page via WebFetch (else `could not read`). Label official vs predicted.
- **Monthly build from your sets**: run `fetch`, then coverage of 1 to 3 saved MOCs against owned sets, offline; API alternates only with a key.

